also large but with a lower bound below threshold. H68/R61 within feature_042=0 is positive but not significant (+0.0165, -0.0246 to +0.0577). The pattern supports feature_045 as a meaningful outcome_006 predictor in at least parts of the population, but because H67's lower bound is marginally below threshold and because of multiple comparisons, I request validation for H67 rather than accepting it immediately. This also tests whether feature_045 retains an effect outside the accepted extreme feature_027/outcome_014 structure.\n\nFeature_054 is not supported as an independent outcome_008 predictor. H70/R63 within feature_042=0 is below threshold (+0.0199, -0.0079 to +0.0478), and H71/R64 within feature_042=1 is null (-0.000014, -0.0451 to +0.0451). I reject and close H71, and because the conditional evidence plus the weak marginal R5 (+0.0146, -0.0091 to +0.0384) does not support the registered outcome_008 association, I reject and close H5. This does not prove zero effect; it means this supplied-dataset evidence is not sufficient to sustain the candidate association after conditioning. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims, and the conditional nulls for feature_042 argue against treating it as a broad predictor even though the accepted feature_042-within-feature_027=1 subgroup signal is scientifically important.",
