  "narrative": "Synthesis after the newly delivered validation and response-deadline items: I reassessed H102, H82, and H88. The supported dataset-specific picture remains narrow but is slightly more informative for the feature_045/outcome_006 line.\n\nThe clearest accepted association remains H30: within the supplied dataset, feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 is associated with a much weaker-dependency outcome_014 score, signed mean difference +0.796 with discovery interval +0.776 to +0.816 and independent validation +0.792 with interval +0.762 to +0.822. This is vastly above the approximate 10% clinical scale for outcome_014, about +0.0093. The accepted strata H129 and H130 show this persists in both feature_054 levels, so it is robust across that predictor. This is a dataset association only, not causal and not assumed transportable.\n\nH76 remains accepted as a context-level average association: feature_045=1 versus feature_045=0 is associated with stronger-dependency outcome_006 within feature_042=1 and feature_027=0. Discovery was +0.106, clinically meaningful; validation preserved direction and approximate magnitude (+0.099) though its conservative interval was wide. Because H113, the feature_002 interaction, failed independent validation, I continue to interpret H76 only as an average association in that explicit feature_042/feature_027 context, not as a confirmed feature_002-conditional narrow marker.\n\nFor H88, the new validation is directionally supportive and clinically large at the point estimate, though imprecise. H88 tests feature_045=1 versus feature_045=0 on outcome_006 within feature_042=1, feature_027=0, and feature_054=level_001. Discovery R115 was +0.1303 with 95% interval +0.0453 to +0.2154, fully above the approximate outcome_006 threshold of +0.0093. Validation R119 was +0.0986 with conservative interval -0.0370 to +0.2342. The validation point estimate is clinically meaningful and agrees with discovery direction, but the interval is wide enough to include small negative values and values below threshold, mostly because cells are small (62/239). I therefore accept H88 only as a supported average association within that explicit subgroup context in the supplied dataset. I do not accept it as proven effect modification by feature_054, because H89 in feature_054=level_002 remains imprecise and H90 interaction remains unresolved. The scientifically appropriate statement is: within feature_042=1/feature_027=0/feature_054=level_001, feature_045=1 is associated with stronger outcome_006 dependency; the evidence is sufficient for a subgroup-specific average association but not sufficient to declare a validated homogeneous or interaction-level feature_054 modification.\n\nFor H102, the original feature_002=0 subgroup contrast in the H76 context had very large discovery evidence, signed estimate +0.2294 with interval +0.1334 to +0.3254. Validation R92 was positive but not confirmatory: point estimate +0.0643, conservative interval -0.0933 to +0.2218. Combined with the failure of H113/H103 interaction validation, I do not accept H102. It remains unresolved but closed: validation did not support the narrow feature_002-conditional interpretation, yet also did not decisively reject the subgroup effect because the interval is wide and the point estimate remains above threshold. The safest interpretation is that H76 is not established as concentrated in feature_002=0.\n\nFor H82, the feature_045/outcome_006 contrast within feature_042=1 and feature_054=level_002 is now clearly unsupported. Discovery R71 was wide and not clinically confirmatory, and validation R93 was near null: signed estimate +0.0047 with conservative interval -0.1955 to +0.2048. I keep H82 rejected and closed. This is an independent failure for that narrow level_002 context, but it does not overturn H76 or H88 because those are different contexts.\n\nThe main negative/unsupported lines are: H60 feature_042/outcome_008 within feature_027=1 after validation reversal; H113/H103 feature_002 interaction modification of H76 after validation reversal; H82 feature_045/outcome_006 in feature_042=1/feature_054=level_002; the broad feature_027 positive claims on several other outcomes that were rejected; and many broad binary screens that showed near-null effects. The feature_042/outcome_001 line remains unsupported overall because the feature_027=1 complement H128 was near null and the earlier feature_027=0 signal remains imprecise and unresolved.\n\nThe main unresolved uncertainty is not whether H88 has a large positive discovery signal, but whether the H76/H88 feature_045/outcome_006 association is outcome-specific and whether feature_054 truly modifies it. H89 and H90 are the direct feature_054 complement/interaction checks but are small and imprecise. H126, H127, H91, and H92 probe broader context and outcome specificity but have not produced clinically decisive evidence. Therefore, the most informative next analyses are the cross-outcome checks of feature_045 within the now-accepted H88 subgroup: outcome_014 and outcome_013 in feature_042=1/feature_027=0/feature_054=level_001. These use the same H88 context and test whether feature_045 has a broader dependency-score signature or is specific to outcome_006. Existing registered comparisons H89, H90, H92, H126, H127, and H91 should also remain candidates for analysis to refine context and complement evidence. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations only; they should not be described as causal, mechanistically validated, or generally generalizable.",
