  "narrative": "The evidence base now contains one highly robust dataset association: feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 is associated with a much weaker-dependency outcome_014 score, with the accepted effect persisting in both feature_054 levels. It also contains two narrower feature_045 lines: feature_045=1 versus feature_045=0 is associated with stronger-dependency outcome_006 within feature_042=1 and feature_027=0, and an accepted subgroup-specific average association within feature_054=level_001. The main uncertainties are whether feature_045 affects other dependency scores in that same context, whether feature_054 truly modifies the feature_045 signal, whether the earlier feature_042 signal on outcome_001 is real and feature_027-specific, and whether feature_042 itself modifies the H76 feature_045/outcome_006 association. I propose four to five targeted follow-up comparisons rather than broad screens. First, I test outcome_001 in the accepted H88 context, feature_042=1, feature_027=0, and feature_054=level_001. Because more negative dependency scores mean stronger dependency, I use direction -1; a positive signed estimate would indicate that feature_045=1 is associated with stronger outcome_001 dependency, while a small or null estimate would support outcome_006 specificity rather than a broad dependency-score signature. Second, I test a direct feature_027 modification interaction for feature_042 on outcome_001, expecting the stronger-dependency feature_042 effect to be larger in the feature_027=0 stratum based on the earlier H112 signal and near-null H128 complement. Third, I test whether feature_042 modifies feature_045 on outcome_006 within feature_027=0. This is the most direct registered-style test of whether the accepted H76 association is truly enhanced in feature_042=1 or whether feature_045 has a broader feature_027=0 association, as the complement H126 has a positive but imprecise point estimate. Fourth, I test feature_045 on outcome_014 and outcome_013 within the H88 complement context, feature_042=1, feature_027=0, and feature_054=level_002. Together with active H134/H135 in level_001 and active H89/H90, this asks whether feature_054 modifies not only outcome_006 but also cross-outcome feature_045 associations. Small cells in level_002 limit precision, so these should be interpreted cautiously. I reopened H89 and H90 as active because H88 is now an accepted subgroup-specific average association and feature_054 modification remains a key unresolved question. All proposals are comparisons in the supplied dataset only; acceptance would mean a dataset association, not causality or generalizability. The clinical scale is roughly a 10% change on each outcome scale, and because these claims use direction -1, a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw exposed-minus-comparator reduction in the dependency score, i.e., stronger dependency.",
